<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="es">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>RWAgallery.art — Obra</title>

    <style>
        body {
            margin: 0;
            padding: 20px;
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            background: #0b0b0f;
            color: #f5f5f5;
            line-height: 1.6;
        }

        h1, h2 {
            color: #ffffff;
        }

        .lang-switch {
            display: flex;
            gap: 10px;
            margin-bottom: 20px;
        }

        button {
            background: #14141a;
            color: #f5f5f5;
            border: 1px solid #333;
            padding: 6px 12px;
            cursor: pointer;
        }

        button.disabled {
            opacity: 0.4;
            cursor: default;
        }

        .layout {
            display: grid;
            grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.4fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
            gap: 24px;
        }

        .card {
            background: #111118;
            border: 1px solid #333;
            border-radius: 8px;
            padding: 16px;
            margin-bottom: 20px;
        }

        .art-image {
            width: 100%;
            border-radius: 8px;
            border: 1px solid #333;
            object-fit: cover;
        }

        .meta-row {
            display: flex;
            justify-content: space-between;
            font-size: 0.9rem;
            opacity: 0.8;
            margin-top: 8px;
        }

        .label {
            font-weight: bold;
        }

        .section-title {
            margin-top: 0;
        }

        .status-tag {
            font-size: 0.85rem;
            opacity: 0.8;
        }

        .wallets {
            display: flex;
            flex-wrap: wrap;
            gap: 8px;
            margin-top: 10px;
        }
    </style>
</head>

<body>

<div class="lang-switch">
    <button id="btn-es">ES</button>
    <button id="btn-en">EN</button>
</div>

<div id="artwork-content">

    <!-- ESPAÑOL -->
    <div id="artwork-es">

        <h1 data-i18n="title_es">Transmutación I</h1>
        <p data-i18n="subtitle_es">
            Obra física vinculada a identidad criptográfica dentro del protocolo RWAgallery.art.
        </p>

        <div class="layout">

            <!-- Columna izquierda: imagen y ficha técnica -->
            <div>

                <div class="card">
                    <img src="https://picsum.photos/800/600?random=10" alt="Transmutación I" class="art-image">

                    <div class="meta-row">
                        <span class="label" data-i18n="artist_label_es">Artista:</span>
                        <span data-i18n="artist_name_es">FDaniel</span>
                    </div>

                    <div class="meta-row">
                        <span class="label" data-i18n="technique_label_es">Técnica:</span>
                        <span data-i18n="technique_es">Mixta sobre soporte rígido</span>
                    </div>

                    <div class="meta-row">
                        <span class="label" data-i18n="size_label_es">Medidas:</span>
                        <span data-i18n="size_es">80 x 60 cm</span>
                    </div>

                    <div class="meta-row">
                        <span class="label" data-i18n="year_label_es">Año:</span>
                        <span data-i18n="year_es">2026</span>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="card">
                    <h2 class="section-title" data-i18n="desc_title_es">Descripción</h2>
                    <p data-i18n="desc_es">
                        Pieza que explora la relación entre luz y materia en un entorno liminal,
                        donde la presencia física de la obra se extiende hacia el espacio criptográfico.
                    </p>
                </div>

            </div>

            <!-- Columna derecha: NFT, RWA y transmutación -->
            <div>

                <div class="card">
                    <h2 class="section-title" data-i18n="nft_title_es">Identidad criptográfica (NFT)</h2>
                    <p class="status-tag" data-i18n="nft_status_es">
                        Estado: vinculación activa en entorno de pruebas (testnet).
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        <span class="label" data-i18n="nft_id_label_es">ID del NFT:</span>
                        <span>0xABCDEF123456</span>
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        <span class="label" data-i18n="network_label_es">Red:</span>
                        <span data-i18n="network_es">Polkadot (preparado para expansión a Ethereum)</span>
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        <span class="label" data-i18n="hash_label_es">Hash de verificación:</span>
                        <span>0xHASH_DE_EJEMPLO</span>
                    </p>
                </div>

                <div class="card">
                    <h2 class="section-title" data-i18n="rwa_title_es">Estado RWA (obra física)</h2>
                    <p data-i18n="rwa_desc_es">
                        La obra física se encuentra registrada en el protocolo RWAgallery.art y puede ser reclamada
                        mediante la identidad criptográfica asociada (NFT).
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        <span class="label" data-i18n="custody_label_es">Custodia actual:</span>
                        <span data-i18n="custody_es">Artista / estudio</span>
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        <span class="label" data-i18n="claim_status_label_es">Estado de reclamación:</span>
                        <span data-i18n="claim_status_es">Disponible para futura transmutación</span>
                    </p>

                    <button class="disabled" style="margin-top: 10px;">
                        <span data-i18n="claim_button_es">Reclamar obra física (desactivado)</span>
                    </button>
                </div>

                <div class="card">
                    <h2 class="section-title" data-i18n="wallets_title_es">Wallets previstas</h2>
                    <p data-i18n="wallets_desc_es">
                        Estas wallets podrán utilizarse en el futuro para verificar la propiedad del NFT y activar la transmutación RWA.
                        De momento, la conexión está desactivada.
                    </p>

                    <div class="wallets">
                        <button class="disabled">
                            Nova / Talisman / Subwallet
                        </button>
                        <button class="disabled">
                            Metamask / Rabby
                        </button>
                    </div>
                </div>

            </div>

        </div>

    </div>

    <!-- ENGLISH -->
    <div id="artwork-en" style="display:none;">

        <h1 data-i18n="title_en">Transmutation I</h1>
        <p data-i18n="subtitle_en">
            Physical artwork linked to cryptographic identity within the RWAgallery.art protocol.
        </p>

        <div class="layout">

            <!-- Left column: image and technical sheet -->
            <div>

                <div class="card">
                    <img src="https://picsum.photos/800/600?random=10" alt="Transmutation I" class="art-image">

                    <div class="meta-row">
                        <span class="label" data-i18n="artist_label_en">Artist:</span>
                        <span data-i18n="artist_name_en">FDaniel</span>
                    </div>

                    <div class="meta-row">
                        <span class="label" data-i18n="technique_label_en">Technique:</span>
                        <span data-i18n="technique_en">Mixed media on rigid support</span>
                    </div>

                    <div class="meta-row">
                        <span class="label" data-i18n="size_label_en">Size:</span>
                        <span data-i18n="size_en">80 x 60 cm</span>
                    </div>

                    <div class="meta-row">
                        <span class="label" data-i18n="year_label_en">Year:</span>
                        <span data-i18n="year_en">2026</span>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="card">
                    <h2 class="section-title" data-i18n="desc_title_en">Description</h2>
                    <p data-i18n="desc_en">
                        Piece exploring the relationship between light and matter in a liminal environment,
                        where the physical presence of the artwork extends into the cryptographic space.
                    </p>
                </div>

            </div>

            <!-- Right column: NFT, RWA and transmutation -->
            <div>

                <div class="card">
                    <h2 class="section-title" data-i18n="nft_title_en">Cryptographic Identity (NFT)</h2>
                    <p class="status-tag" data-i18n="nft_status_en">
                        Status: active linkage in testing environment (testnet).
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        <span class="label" data-i18n="nft_id_label_en">NFT ID:</span>
                        <span>0xABCDEF123456</span>
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        <span class="label" data-i18n="network_label_en">Network:</span>
                        <span data-i18n="network_en">Polkadot (prepared for expansion to Ethereum)</span>
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        <span class="label" data-i18n="hash_label_en">Verification hash:</span>
                        <span>0xHASH_EXAMPLE</span>
                    </p>
                </div>

                <div class="card">
                    <h2 class="section-title" data-i18n="rwa_title_en">RWA Status (physical artwork)</h2>
                    <p data-i18n="rwa_desc_en">
                        The physical artwork is registered within the RWAgallery.art protocol and may be claimed
                        through its associated cryptographic identity (NFT).
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        <span class="label" data-i18n="custody_label_en">Current custody:</span>
                        <span data-i18n="custody_en">Artist / studio</span>
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        <span class="label" data-i18n="claim_status_label_en">Claim status:</span>
                        <span data-i18n="claim_status_en">Available for future transmutation</span>
                    </p>

                    <button class="disabled" style="margin-top: 10px;">
                        <span data-i18n="claim_button_en">Claim physical artwork (disabled)</span>
                    </button>
                </div>

                <div class="card">
                    <h2 class="section-title" data-i18n="wallets_title_en">Planned wallets</h2>
                    <p data-i18n="wallets_desc_en">
                        These wallets will be used in the future to verify NFT ownership and activate RWA transmutation.
                        For now, connection is disabled.
                    </p>

                    <div class="wallets">
                        <button class="disabled">
                            Nova / Talisman / Subwallet
                        </button>
                        <button class="disabled">
                            Metamask / Rabby
                        </button>
                    </div>
                </div>

            </div>

        </div>

    </div>

</div>

<script>
    document.getElementById("btn-es").addEventListener("click", () => {
        document.getElementById("artwork-es").style.display = "block";
        document.getElementById("artwork-en").style.display = "none";
    });

    document.getElementById("btn-en").addEventListener("click", () => {
        document.getElementById("artwork-es").style.display = "none";
        document.getElementById("artwork-en").style.display = "block";
    });
</script>

</body>
</html>
